{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Arrival feels like a natural next choice because first contact and communication connect with the interest suggested by my Star Trek interaction.",
    "Blade Runner 2049 interests me for its questions about identity, and The Tomorrow War also appeals as science fiction, though Arrival fits my mood best."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Commuter and Aquaman offer action or adventure, but those qualities alone do not satisfy my current interest in speculative ideas.",
    "Sully's real-world aviation story does not match what I want now, and I cannot judge whether the untitled items match my interests without knowing what they are."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to stretch my interest in science fiction into a broader interest in action and spectacle.",
    "Treating these films as similarly appealing misses why stories about communication or identity interest me more than a thriller or real-world drama."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Right now, thoughtful speculative themes matter more to me than excitement alone; that is why I would choose Arrival first.",
    "Tone affects my choice within science fiction: Blade Runner 2049 interests me, but its darker tone makes me less certain. My one named Star Trek interaction is only a limited clue to my preferences."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognize my current interest in science fiction but extend it too broadly to action and drama while missing the themes and tone that drive my choices."
}"}
